<title>DENMARK: Danish November consumer confidence +6 (Oct +5).</title>
<headline>Danish November consumer confidence +6 (Oct +5).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's consumer confidence indicator was +6 in November, up from +5 in October 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>		   Nov 96	    Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p>		    +6		   +5		 +9</p>
<p>NOTE: The survey asks a cross section of Denmark's population its views on current personal and national economic trends, along with consumer intentions for coming months. Changes in consumer confidence are indicated by a higher or lower weighted rating, rather than by index.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969650</p>
